{"id":"e824a8435bba9f97","group":"58","path":"58/batch09/58-df-nuclear-norm.md","title":"Nuclear Norm","display":"df-nuclear-norm — Nuclear Norm","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-nuclear-norm","aliases":["58-df-nuclear-norm","Nuclear Norm"],"display":"df-nuclear-norm — Nuclear Norm","depends_on":["[[58-df-singular-value]]","[[../batch13/58-df-hilbert-space.md]]","[[../batch03/58-df-compact-operator.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-nuclear-norm"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-nuclear-norm</span><span>Nuclear Norm</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-nuclear-norm — Nuclear Norm"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"7da7ff11e397ca55\" href=\"?note=7da7ff11e397ca55\" title=\"58-df-singular-value\">58-df-singular-value</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"b70ce791d5b1a19b\" href=\"?note=b70ce791d5b1a19b\" title=\"../batch13/58-df-hilbert-space.md\">../batch13/58-df-hilbert-space.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"28999e0c83253377\" href=\"?note=28999e0c83253377\" title=\"../batch03/58-df-compact-operator.md\">../batch03/58-df-compact-operator.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"H_1,H_2,\\langle\\cdot,\\cdot\\rangle_1,\\langle\\cdot,\\cdot\\rangle_2,T,r\\in V\">\\(H_1,H_2,\\langle\\cdot,\\cdot\\rangle_1,\\langle\\cdot,\\cdot\\rangle_2,T,r\\in V\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{HilbertSpace}_S\\subseteq V^2\">\\(\\mathrm{HilbertSpace}_S\\subseteq V^2\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{CompactOperator}_S\\subseteq V^3\">\\(\\mathrm{CompactOperator}_S\\subseteq V^3\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{SingularValue}_S\\subseteq V^5\">\\(\\mathrm{SingularValue}_S\\subseteq V^5\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{NuclearNorm}_S\\subseteq V^6\">\\(\\mathrm{NuclearNorm}_S\\subseteq V^6\\)</span></li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}nuclear\\text{-}norm}\\vdash{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{NuclearNorm}_S(r,T,H_1,\\langle\\cdot,\\cdot\\rangle_1,H_2,\\langle\\cdot,\\cdot\\rangle_2)\\\\\n\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{HilbertSpace}_S(H_1,\\langle\\cdot,\\cdot\\rangle_1)\n\\land\\mathrm{HilbertSpace}_S(H_2,\\langle\\cdot,\\cdot\\rangle_2)\n\\land\\mathrm{CompactOperator}_S(T,H_1,H_2)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\exists s\\in V\\;\\bigl(\n\\mathrm{Function}(s,\\omega,\\mathbb R_{\\geq0})\n\\land\\forall n\\in\\omega\\;\n\\mathrm{SingularValue}_S(s(n),n+1,T,H_1,H_2)\n\\land r=\\sum_{n\\in\\omega}s(n)\\bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}nuclear\\text{-}norm}\\vdash{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{NuclearNorm}_S(r,T,H_1,\\langle\\cdot,\\cdot\\rangle_1,H_2,\\langle\\cdot,\\cdot\\rangle_2)\\\\\n\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{HilbertSpace}_S(H_1,\\langle\\cdot,\\cdot\\rangle_1)\n\\land\\mathrm{HilbertSpace}_S(H_2,\\langle\\cdot,\\cdot\\rangle_2)\n\\land\\mathrm{CompactOperator}_S(T,H_1,H_2)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\exists s\\in V\\;\\bigl(\n\\mathrm{Function}(s,\\omega,\\mathbb R_{\\geq0})\n\\land\\forall n\\in\\omega\\;\n\\mathrm{SingularValue}_S(s(n),n+1,T,H_1,H_2)\n\\land r=\\sum_{n\\in\\omega}s(n)\\bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The nuclear norm is the (possibly infinite) sum of singular values; it is finite exactly for trace-class operators between Hilbert spaces.</li>\n<li>Duality: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\|T\\|_* = \\sup\\{|\\operatorname{Tr}(T S)| : \\|S\\| \\leq 1\\}\">\\(\\|T\\|_* = \\sup\\{|\\operatorname{Tr}(T S)| : \\|S\\| \\leq 1\\}\\)</span>; operator norm dual</li>\n<li>Matrix: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\|*\\|_*\">\\(\\|*\\|_*\\)</span> convex; nuclear norm approximation for rank minimization</li>\n<li>SVD: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\|T\\|_* = \\sum \\sigma_i\">\\(\\|T\\|_* = \\sum \\sigma_i\\)</span>; nuclear norm vs operator norm <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\|T\\| = \\sigma_1\">\\(\\|T\\| = \\sigma_1\\)</span></li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Reed and Simon, Functional Analysis</li>\n<li>Pietsch, Operator Ideals</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-singular-value","status":"resolved","id":"7da7ff11e397ca55","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-singular-value]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch13/58-df-hilbert-space.md","status":"resolved","id":"b70ce791d5b1a19b","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch13/58-df-hilbert-space.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch03/58-df-compact-operator.md","status":"resolved","id":"28999e0c83253377","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch03/58-df-compact-operator.md]]","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"H_1,H_2,\\langle\\cdot,\\cdot\\rangle_1,\\langle\\cdot,\\cdot\\rangle_2,T,r\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{HilbertSpace}_S\\subseteq V^2","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{CompactOperator}_S\\subseteq V^3","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{SingularValue}_S\\subseteq V^5","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{NuclearNorm}_S\\subseteq V^6","display":false},{"tex":"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}nuclear\\text{-}norm}\\vdash{}&\n\\mathrm{NuclearNorm}_S(r,T,H_1,\\langle\\cdot,\\cdot\\rangle_1,H_2,\\langle\\cdot,\\cdot\\rangle_2)\\\\\n\\leftrightarrow{}&\n\\mathrm{HilbertSpace}_S(H_1,\\langle\\cdot,\\cdot\\rangle_1)\n\\land\\mathrm{HilbertSpace}_S(H_2,\\langle\\cdot,\\cdot\\rangle_2)\n\\land\\mathrm{CompactOperator}_S(T,H_1,H_2)\\\\\n&\\land\\exists s\\in V\\;\\bigl(\n\\mathrm{Function}(s,\\omega,\\mathbb R_{\\geq0})\n\\land\\forall n\\in\\omega\\;\n\\mathrm{SingularValue}_S(s(n),n+1,T,H_1,H_2)\n\\land r=\\sum_{n\\in\\omega}s(n)\\bigr).\n\\end{aligned}","display":true},{"tex":"\\|T\\|_* = \\sup\\{|\\operatorname{Tr}(T S)| : \\|S\\| \\leq 1\\}","display":false},{"tex":"\\|*\\|_*","display":false},{"tex":"\\|T\\|_* = \\sum \\sigma_i","display":false},{"tex":"\\|T\\| = \\sigma_1","display":false}],"bytes":1659,"backlinks":[{"id":"d4d317c47fe1ba6e","anchor":"ref-2","locations":["元数据 · depends_on","正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"$\\mathrm{NuclearNorm}_S:V^6\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}$ is the Hilbert-space nuclear-norm predicate from [[../batch09/58-df-nuclear-norm.md]]."},{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-892","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch09/58-df-nuclear-norm.md|58-df-nuclear-norm]]（batch09）"}],"outgoing":["7da7ff11e397ca55","b70ce791d5b1a19b","28999e0c83253377"]}